  +  attention
    '  The world's attention: one crew over every name its cursors
    '  hold.  A held name is a slot ['held …name] whose text is the
    '  cursors holding it (relative paths, space-separated).  When a
    '  held name moves (at care z: the name or anything beneath it),
    '  each cursor holding it is poked asking.  The edge reads which
    '  cursors ask and runs them; nothing here says what a cursor does.
    +  rest
      '  A path without its first segment.
      \  p=path
      ^  path
      %  i=nat 1  q=path []
      ^  path
      ?  (ge i p.len)  q
      (_ i.inc q.snoc(p.at(i)))
    +  top_of
      '  The crew key for a held slot: its name's first segment.  The
      '  crew watches tops (a doc, a folder) at z, a few hunts however
      '  many names are held; hear finds the exact holders by lookup.
      \  key=path
      ^  path
      =  held=path ['held]
      held.weld((hands/attention/rest key).take(1))
    +  hunt_for
      '  The hunt a crew key stands for: that top, in this world, at z.
      \  home=path key=path
      ^  dep
      (dep .z home.weld((hands/attention/rest key)))
    +  aim
      '  The crew built whole: a hunt per held slot with holders.
      \  b=bowl t=myth
      ^  myth
      =  es t.tap
         home b.here.take(1)
      %  i=nat 0  c=crew (myth/crew_at crew_slot t).filter((\ k v .false))
      ^  myth
      ?  (ge i es.len)  t.put(crew_slot (cpail c))
      =  e es.at(i)
      ?  !(pith_prefix ['held] e.key)  (_ i.inc c)
      ?  (eq 0 (myth/txt_at e.key t).len)  (_ i.inc c)
      =  top (hands/attention/top_of e.key)
      (_ i.inc c.put(top (hands/attention/hunt_for home top)))
    +  init
      \  b=bowl t=myth
      ^  yell
      |  yell [] (hands/attention/aim b t)
    +  talk
      '  Held slots poked in: the crew rebuilt from every held slot
      '  (a hunt per top: cheap, and a top emptied of holders drops).
      \  b=bowl cur=myth nu=myth
      ^  yell
      =  d (def_talk b cur nu)
      |  yell d.cards (hands/attention/aim b d.out)
    +  pokes
      '  A card per holder: that cursor poked asking.
      \  home=path who=row[str] cards=row[[p=path q=writ]]
      ^  row[[p=path q=writ]]
      %  j=nat 0  cs=row[[p=path q=writ]] cards
      ^  row[[p=path q=writ]]
      ?  (ge j who.len)  cs
      ?>  (./some c) (path_parse who.at(j))
          (_ j.inc cs)
      (_ j.inc cs.snoc([home.weld(c) (writ/poke (myth/sing ['asking] (pt "yes")))]))
    +  holders
      '  The cards for one moved name: the holders of it and of every
      '  name above it.
      \  home=path cur=myth name=path cards=row[[p=path q=writ]]
      ^  row[[p=path q=writ]]
      %  k=nat 1  cs=row[[p=path q=writ]] cards
      ^  row[[p=path q=writ]]
      ?  (gt k name.len)  cs
      =  held=path ['held]
      =  who (str/split_byte 32 (myth/txt_at held.weld(name.take(k)) cur))
      (_ k.inc (hands/attention/pokes home who cs))
    +  hear
      '  Names moved: every cursor holding one, or a name above one, is
      '  poked asking.
      \  b=bowl cur=myth r=row[dep]
      ^  yell
      =  home b.here.take(1)
      %  i=nat 0  cards=row[[p=path q=writ]] []
      ^  yell
      ?  (ge i r.len)  (yell cards cur)
      =  moved (hands/attention/rest r.at(i).p)
      (_ i.inc (hands/attention/holders home cur moved cards))
    +  form
      ^  form
      def_form.set_init(hands/attention/init).set_talk(hands/attention/talk).set_hear(hands/attention/hear)
